# Typography — all VTC apps (mandatory)

**One hierarchy** for shell (posif-svelte), iframe child apps (Next / Vite + `@vtc/ui`), and new rebuilds. Do not invent per-app type scales.

## Semantic roles (use these names in reviews and PRs)

| Role | Size / weight | Use for |
|------|----------------|---------|
| **caption** | `text-xs`, muted | Hints, counts, timestamps, subtext |
| **body** | `text-sm` | Paragraphs, menu items, default list copy |
| **label** | `text-sm font-medium` | Form labels, secondary header actions |
| **section** | `text-sm font-semibold` | Structural headings **inside a panel** (not the active tab name) |
| **tab-primary** | `text-sm font-semibold` | Primary tab row (Home / Apps / Members, main nav tabs) |
| **tab-secondary** | `text-xs font-semibold` | Nested tabs under a primary tab |
| **row-title** | `text-sm font-semibold` | List/card row titles (names, app rows) |
| **row-meta** | `text-xs`, muted | @handle, category under a row title |
| **overlay-title** | `text-lg font-semibold` | Modal, sheet, dialog, standalone app bar title |
| **display-sm** / **display** | `text-xl` / `text-2xl` semibold/bold | **Marketing / public landings only** — not product shell |
| **input-emphasis** | `text-base font-semibold` | **Native inputs only** (avoid iOS zoom-on-focus) |

## Hierarchy rules (all apps)

1. **In-panel structure must not exceed `section` / `tab-primary` (`text-sm` semibold)** except **overlay-title** (modals) or documented **display** / stat emphasis.
2. **Do not repeat the active tab name** as a second heading in the same panel.
3. **Sub-tabs** use **tab-secondary** — smaller than primary tabs.
4. **Headings** (`h1`–`h6`) need explicit size/weight classes — never UA defaults.
5. **No ad-hoc `text-xl` / `text-2xl` page titles** in embedded child apps; shell chrome already names the app. **Never** render the app name as a home heading or subtitle ("Your personal X") when embedded — home starts with content/actions (`ui.mdc` § Platform shell chrome). Nested screen titles are fine.
6. **Font family:** platform system stack or network `typography=` / `font=` via `ThemeProvider` — `network-branding.mdc`, `ui.mdc` § font family.

## Implementation by stack

### posif-svelte (main shell)

- **Spec copy in repo:** `docs/typography.md` (must match this file).
- **CSS:** `src/lib/styles/typography.css` — classes `type-caption`, `type-body`, `type-label`, `type-section`, `type-tab-primary`, `type-tab-secondary`, `type-row-title`, `type-row-meta`, `type-overlay-title`, `type-display-sm`, `type-display`, `type-input-emphasis`.
- Prefer `type-*` over raw Tailwind in `src/**/*.svelte`.

### Next.js / static Vite + `@vtc/ui` (**required for new / rebuilt apps**)

1. **`@vtc/ui` ≥ 1.3.0** in `package.json`.
2. In `globals.css` (after Tailwind `@import`):

```css
@import "@vtc/ui/typography.css";
```

3. Use **`type-*` classes** or exported components / `typeClass`:

```tsx
import { SectionHeading, BodyText, OverlayTitle, typeClass } from '@vtc/ui'
```

| Class / `typeClass` | Role |
|---------------------|------|
| `type-caption` | caption |
| `type-body` | body |
| `type-label` | label |
| `type-section` | section |
| `type-tab-primary` / `type-tab-secondary` | tabs |
| `type-row-title` / `type-row-meta` | list rows |
| `type-overlay-title` | modals, standalone bar title |
| `type-display-sm` / `type-display` | marketing only |
| `type-input-emphasis` | native inputs only |

Do **not** hand-compose `text-2xl` page titles. `PageTitle` in `@vtc/ui` is an alias for **overlay-title** scale.

**Embedded in platform shell:** sticky header is **actions only** — use **section** inside `<main>`.

### Buttons

`text-sm font-medium` on button labels — `ui.mdc` § Buttons.

## Weights

- **semibold** — section, tabs, row titles, overlay titles.
- **medium** — labels, default buttons.
- **bold** — primary **Button** component and **display** marketing only.

## Audit (posif-svelte)

```bash
./scripts/typography-audit.sh
```

Child apps: grep for `text-2xl`, `text-xl font-bold` on in-app headings and replace with **section** / **overlay-title** per table above.

## Related rules

- `ui.mdc` — App Shell, theme, accent, components (defers to this file for type hierarchy).
- `i18n.mdc` — translated strings; no impact on scale.
